  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A closed tube filled with water is rotating uniformly in a horizontal plane about the axis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>O</mi><mo>'</mo></math>&nbsp;as shown in the figure. The manometers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;which are&nbsp;fixed on the&nbsp;tube at distances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, indicate pressures&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively. The angular velocity (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ω</mi></math>) of the tube is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/129027_adjjavda_v.png\" style=\"width: 225px; height: 218px;\" /></p>\r",
